 The whole game, folded: one ride state, one step of it, and one frame drawn from
 it. A port of wasm/safari.zig, and the last file in the game to be ported.

 safari.zig is the module the browser sees, and most of it is an ABI -- twenty
 exports handing the blitter numbers it cannot compute. THREE THINGS IN IT ARE NOT
 ABI, and those are what this chapter is:

   THE STATE FOLD. advance() is four calls in a fixed order and a restart at the
     finish line. The order is the whole content: the truck steps against the NEW
     rider distance, because its schedule anchors to where the rider is now.
   THE FRAME. renderFrame() computes the live focal and the view yaw, then calls
     render.frame -- whose outer sequence (backdrop, ground, everything that
     stands up in depth order) had lived in the browser poc because half its
     drawers were unported. They are all ported now, so it belongs here, above
     Render rather than inside it: the dispatch has to cite every drawer, and
     TruckDraw cites Render, so a dispatch inside Render would be a cycle.
   THE CAMERA PULL-IN. The lens narrows as he leans and as he watches a crossing
     cat. `cam-focal`, `focal-for-lean` and `focal-for-gaze` have been ported and
     idle since Camera landed, because nothing above them existed to compute the
     two fractions they take. This is that thing.

 WHAT STAYS OUTSIDE, and it is a short list: the history ring, the exports, and
 the mutable statics that hold the current ride. Those are the shim's, and the
 shim is where they belong -- a Codex program is pure and a ring buffer is not.
 What the shim loses by this chapter existing is all the LOGIC it used to carry:
 the restart, the step order, the focal, the view-yaw fold. It keeps a value, an
 array and twenty exported readouts.

 We say:

Section: The Ride

 ONE RECORD FOR THE WHOLE RIDE, because the three things advance together and a
 caller that could step one without the others would be a bug waiting. The clock
 is a plain frame count -- safari.zig's `step_clock`, which gains one per advance
 and gives one back on the way out -- and it drives the sunset, the sun and the
 tower beacons.

  Ride = record {
    rider : RiderState,
    truck : TruckState,
    clock : Real
  }

  ride-initial : Ride
  ride-initial = Ride { rider = initial-rider-state, truck = truck-initial, clock = 0.0 }

 ONE STEP, AND THE ORDER IN IT IS THE WHOLE CONTENT. The rider moves first and the
 truck steps against his NEW route distance, because the chase schedule anchors to
 where he is now; stepping it against the old distance would leave the lead one
 frame stale at exactly the moments it is tightest. The finish line restarts the
 whole ride rather than stopping, because this is a screensaver.

  ride-next : List Segment, Ride -> Ride
  ride-next (w) (r) =
    if is-finished r.rider w then ride-initial else ride-step w r

  ride-step : List Segment, Ride -> Ride
  ride-step (w) (r) =
    let nx = get-next-rider-state r.rider w
    in let dist = route-distance w nx.segment nx.along
    in Ride { rider = nx, truck = truck-next r.truck dist w (course-length w), clock = r.clock + 1.0 }

Section: The Frame

 render.zig's own sequence: the backdrop behind everything, then the floor, then
 everything that stands up, in one depth order. The live focal reaches all three.

  ride-frame : List Segment, Ride -> List DrawCmd
  ride-frame (w) (r) =
    let s = r.rider
    in let cf = ride-focal w s
    in let vy = view-yaw-for s
    in let pose = pose-for w s
    in let ch = build-chain w s.segment
    in (draw (s.heading + vy) (sun-set-fraction r.clock) cf camera-w)
       & (frame-ground w s.segment pose cf camera-w)
       & (draw-order w ch pose (collect w s.segment pose cf s.along s.v r.truck.pos) r.truck.braking cf r.clock 0)

 The sun's placement for this frame, which the blitter paints itself behind the
 ranges. It reads the same heading the mountains do and the same live focal the
 rest of the frame does, so it cannot drift away from what is drawn over it.

  ride-sun : List Segment, Ride -> SunPos
  ride-sun (w) (r) =
    let cf = ride-focal w r.rider
    in sun-pos (heading-for r.rider) r.clock cf camera-w
